  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 304.31 Certification Committee",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 304.31 Certification Committee. The certification committee serves as the review committee for certification of wastewater treatment plant operators, and shall be comprised as follows:\n\n(a) Three certified operators designated by the director of the department’s division of water, no more than 2 of which shall be employed by the department;\n\n(b) Two certified operators shall be elected by the New Hampshire Water Pollution Control Association as specified in RSA 485-A:2, I-b, provided that the designated individuals elected shall hold a current New Hampshire wastewater treatment plant operator certification pursuant to these rules; and\n\n(c) Two certified operators designated by the director of the department's division of water, one of which shall be designated as the primary alternate, and the other designated as the secondary alternate, to sit in place of a member(s) designated in (a) or (b) above, in the event that a member(s) is unavailable.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at part heading for Env-Wq 304) #10392, eff 8-1-13; ss by #13755, eff 9-27-23 (see Revision Note #2 at part heading for Env-Wq 304)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq300.html"
